{"name":"Jet","hex":"#343434","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Jet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Oklahoma.","A male given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Jet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jet aircraft","blocks":[{"text":"A jet aircraft is an aircraft propelled by one or more jet engines. Jets are nearly always fixed-wing aircraft, though a wide range of different types of jet aircraft exists – both for civilian and military purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/BEA_de_Havilland_DH-106_Comet_4B_Berlin.jpg/330px-BEA_de_Havilland_DH-106_Comet_4B_Berlin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet_aircraft","wikidata":"Q206592"},{"title":"Jet engine","blocks":[{"text":"A jet engine is a type of reaction engine, discharging a fast-moving jet of heated gas that generates thrust by jet propulsion. While this broad definition may include rocket, water jet, and hybrid propulsion, the term jet engine typically refers to an internal combustion air-breathing jet engine such as a turbojet, turbofan, ramjet, pulse jet, or scramjet. In general, jet engines are internal combustion engines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/F100_F-15_engine.JPG/330px-F100_F-15_engine.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet_engine","wikidata":"Q178777"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Ohain_USAF_He_178_page61.jpg/500px-Ohain_USAF_He_178_page61.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Ohain_USAF_He_178_page61.jpg/500px-Ohain_USAF_He_178_page61.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Heinkel He 178 was the first aircraft t